Q1. What is Docker?
Ans. Docker is a platform for packaging and running applications in isolated containers.

Q2. What is a Docker image?
Ans. A Docker image is a template used to create containers.

Q3. What is a Docker container?
Ans. A container is a running instance of a Docker image.

Q4. What is a Dockerfile?
Ans. A Dockerfile contains instructions for building a Docker image.

Q5. Why do we use requirements.txt?
Ans. It lists the Python packages required by the application.

Q6. What is the purpose of docker build?
Ans. It builds a Docker image from a Dockerfile.

Q7. What is the purpose of docker run?
Ans. It creates and starts a container from an image.

Q8. What does port mapping mean?
Ans. It connects a port on the host computer to a port inside the container.

Q9. Why is Docker useful for AI/ML?
Ans. It packages the model application and dependencies so the environment is consistent across machines.

Q10. What is an API?
Ans. An API allows one software application to communicate with another. In this experiment, the API receives input and returns a model prediction.
